    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12789" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕ-haurĭo</span></b>  (also written <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dehōrio</span></b> , like clodo,
			codex, clostrum, plostrum, etc.), hausi, haustum,
		4, v. a.—* <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To skim off</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amurcam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato R.
					R. 66 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To swal</i>
			
			
			<i>low down, to swallow</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">margarita pretiosa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 5 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: carnem, id. Resurr. carn. 11 <i>fin.</i></div>
